  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Joshua",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 4,
    "summary": "Joshua places twelve stones to commemorate the crossing of the Jordan—Joshua is magnified before the children of Israel as they cross the Jordan—After the priests bearing the ark pass over, the river returns to its course.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, when all the people were clean passed over Jordan, that the Lord spake unto Joshua, saying,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "HEB completely."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 4:1",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Take you twelve men out of the people, out of every tribe a man,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Joshua 4:2",
        "book": "Joshua",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And command ye them, saying, Take you hence out of the midst of Jordan, out of the place where the priests’ feet stood firm, twelve stones, and ye shall carry them over with you, and leave them in the lodging place, where ye shall lodge this night.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 131,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 18:31."
          },
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 138,
            "text": "Deut. 27:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
